# installer/theme.manifest
#
# Canonical "complete theme" manifest for a directory under
# $HYDE_CONFIG_HOME/themes/<name>/. A theme directory is only considered
# complete for this installer's purposes if every REQUIRED entry exists.
# Directory existence alone (`themes/<name>/` present) is NOT a valid
# completeness test - see installer/runtime.sh theme_check_complete().
#
# Format (pipe-delimited, '#' comments and blank lines ignored):
#   path | REQUIRED|OPTIONAL | consumed-by | notes
#
# path is relative to the theme directory. A trailing '/' means a
# directory (checked with -d), otherwise checked with -e (file or symlink).

wall.set     | REQUIRED | color.set.sh (theme.switch.sh entry point), wallpaper.sh, globalcontrol.sh:get_themes | symlink to the active wallpaper; color.set.sh's dcol/hash cache and the seed for wallbash template rendering are derived from this
hypr.theme   | REQUIRED | color/hypr.sh (hyq), theme.switch.sh (hyq, load_hypr_variables), globalcontrol.sh:get_hyprConf, waybar.py:get_hypr_theme_setting, wallbash/scripts/swaync.sh | hyprlang-syntax ($KEY = value) theme metadata queried by hyq; see installer/templates/hypr.theme.default for the canonical minimal content this installer writes
.sort        | OPTIONAL | globalcontrol.sh:get_themes | numeric theme-list ordering; defaults to "0" when absent, get_themes never fails without it
wallpapers/  | OPTIONAL | theme.switch.sh (fallback wall.set relink if the existing symlink target is missing) | only consulted when wall.set is a dangling link; a theme that ships wall.set pointing at a real file never needs this
theme.dcol   | OPTIONAL | color.set.sh (dominant-colour override) | when absent, colours are derived from the wallpaper itself instead - documented, intentional fallback, never an error
